      "math_academy_id": "q-225192",
      "sequence_position": 7,
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(7,0.48)$ given below, compute $P(X>5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0103\\,$ | $\\,0.0767\\,$ | $\\,0.2607\\,$ | $\\,0.5437\\,$ | $\\,0.8049\\,$ | $\\,0.9496\\,$ | $\\,0.9941\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |\n\n$P(X>5)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>5) & =1-P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =1-F(5) \\\\  & =1-0.9496 \\\\  & =0.0504.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
